<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  HomeKit entitlement (`com.apple.developer.homekit`) is INTENTIONALLY
  omitted. Apple gates HomeKit capability behind the paid Developer
  Program; including it here would break local builds for contributors
  signing with a personal Apple ID team. Without the entitlement,
  `HMHomeManager` simply reports zero homes and `HomeKitSkill` returns
  `noHomeFound` — already handled gracefully (no crash). To enable
  real HomeKit control, add `<key>com.apple.developer.homekit</key>
  <true/>` below in your local fork and ensure your provisioning
  profile includes the HomeKit capability.

  iOS LLM Optimization: Kernel Entitlements
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  The following entitlements significantly improve LLM performance on
  memory-constrained devices and are STRONGLY RECOMMENDED for production builds:
    - com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit
    - com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing

  ⚠️  These require a PAID Apple Developer account.
  Personal/free developer teams cannot use these entitlements.

  See KERNEL_ENTITLEMENTS.md for setup instructions.

  iCloud Documents Sync
  ─────────────────────
  Enables the `AppSettings.iCloudSyncEnabled` toggle to write the
  FileStore JSON tree into the user's iCloud Drive instead of sandbox-
  local Application Support. Data then survives reinstalls AND syncs
  across the user's iCloud-signed-in devices.

  CONTAINER ID: `iCloud.cz.keksiczek.homehub` — must match a container
  the developer has provisioned in their Apple Developer portal AND
  enabled on the App ID. The free Apple ID flow:
    1. Open Xcode → HomeHub target → Signing & Capabilities → "+ Capability"
    2. Add "iCloud", then check "iCloud Documents" service.
    3. Click "+ Container" under "Containers" and create
       `iCloud.cz.keksiczek.homehub` (or pick your own and update the
       string below).

  If the container isn't provisioned, `forUbiquityContainerIdentifier:`
  returns nil at runtime and the bridge silently falls back to local
  Application Support — the app keeps working, the user just doesn't
  get cross-device sync (and they see "iCloud unavailable" in
  Settings).
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.cz.keksiczek.homehub.shared</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.cz.keksiczek.homehub</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudDocuments</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.cz.keksiczek.homehub</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
